      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. the contrast is definitely there, but maybe a bit too \"polite\" for a satire piece. i want the satire to be a bit more biting and visceral. \n\nfor the local resident, can you make their voice feel a bit more \"authentic\" to the neighborhood? like, lean more into the street-level dialect or the way people actually talk in these older, gritty urban areas. and maybe make the attitude a bit more defensive or even a little aggressive to show how much they feel pushed out. help me make it feel more real, you know?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
